{"architectures":["x86"],"id":"Python.Launcher","latestVersion":"3.15.2","media":{"icons":[{"mimeType":"image/png","path":"media/icon.c1e79d78.png","priority":1,"sha256":"c1e79d7897ee0ee9157b3da8293283f532816682f2d4b1ed1bc23bae44b9db0f","source":"winget-legacy"}],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"author":"Python Software Foundation","copyright":"Copyright (c) 2001-2023 Python Software Foundation. All Rights Reserved.","copyrightUrl":"https://www.python.org/about/legal/","description":"The Python launcher for Windows is a utility which aids in locating and executing of different Python versions.","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"Python Launcher for Windows","DocumentUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3/using/windows.html#launcher"}],"license":"PSF-2.0","licenseUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3/license.html","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"author":"Python Software Foundation","copyright":"Copyright (c) 2001-2023 Python Software Foundation. All Rights Reserved.","copyrightUrl":"https://www.python.org/about/legal/","description":"The Python launcher for Windows is a utility which aids in locating and executing of different Python versions.","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"Python Launcher for Windows","DocumentUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3/using/windows.html#launcher"}],"license":"PSF-2.0","licenseUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3/license.html","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"The Python launcher for Windows is a utility which aids in locating and executing of different Python versions.\nIt allows scripts (or the command-line) to indicate a preference for a specific Python version, and will locate and execute that version.\n\nUnlike the PATH variable, the launcher will correctly select the most appropriate version of Python.\nIt will prefer per-user installations over system-wide ones, and orders by language version rather than using the most recently installed version.\n\nThe launcher was originally specified in PEP 397.","moniker":"python-launcher","name":"Python Launcher","packageUrl":"https://www.python.org/","privacyUrl":"https://www.python.org/privacy/","publisher":"Python Software Foundation","publisherSupportUrl":"https://www.python.org/about/help/","publisherUrl":"https://www.python.org/","tags":["language","programming","programming-language","python","python3","script"]}},"longDescription":"The Python launcher for Windows is a utility which aids in locating and executing of different Python versions.\nIt allows scripts (or the command-line) to indicate a preference for a specific Python version, and will locate and execute that version.\n\nUnlike the PATH variable, the launcher will correctly select the most appropriate version of Python.\nIt will prefer per-user installations over system-wide ones, and orders by language version rather than using the most recently installed version.\n\nThe launcher was originally specified in PEP 397.","moniker":"python-launcher","name":"Python Launcher","packageUrl":"https://www.python.org/","privacyUrl":"https://www.python.org/privacy/","publisher":"Python Software Foundation","publisherSupportUrl":"https://www.python.org/about/help/","publisherUrl":"https://www.python.org/","tags":["language","programming","programming-language","python","python3","script"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["x86"],"detailPath":"versions/3.15.2/app.json","detailSha256":"aac1ef17c0660ed6691a5669fd09f123e0d539edf67588236a4fd870f8745b04","releaseDate":"2026-11-05","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"3.15.2"},{"architectures":["x86"],"detailPath":"versions/3.14.7/app.json","detailSha256":"5244dc9f1a57a31740a3380ec5374f07b78f63aa96b9a8eb3c97db427f970f0f","releaseDate":"2026-08-05","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"3.14.7"},{"architectures":["x86"],"detailPath":"versions/3.13.5/app.json","detailSha256":"6184ab5549c799d6f65ce471e2848be46e3576b7442536c6d4e92fa89b2bb3b5","releaseDate":"2025-06-11","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"3.13.5"},{"archi